":{"fieldSizeRank":33,"finishersRank":31,"finishRateRank":65,"winningTimeRank":27,"winningTimeRankDir":9,"totalRaces":98},"recordContext":{"womenRecords":["up"],"womenPreviousRecord":{"time":"06:13:23","holder":"Ann TRASON","year":1996,"type":"up"},"womenWouldHaveWonMen":{"mostRecentYear":1966,"mensWinner":"Tommy MALONE","mensTime":"06:14:07"}},"narrative":"The 2004 Comrades Marathon was the 79th running of the race, run in the 'up' direction from Durban to Pietermaritzburg over 86.750 km. The race was held on Wednesday, 16 June. Conditions: Cloudless, fine and warm. Runners had 12 hours to complete the course.\n\nVladimir KOTOV claimed the men's title in 05:31:22, ahead of Jaroslaw JANICKI (05:34:17) and Oleg KHARITONOV (05:39:08). Elena NURGALIEVA won the women's race in 06:11:15, followed by Marina ZHALYBINA (06:14:13).\n\nElena NURGALIEVA set a new women's up record of 06:11:15, surpassing Ann TRASON's 06:13:23 from 1996. Elena NURGALIEVA's 06:11:15 was faster than the men's winning time as recently as 1966 (Tommy MALONE, 06:14:07).\n\nFrom a field of 12,049 entries, 10,119 runners crossed the finish line (84.0% completion rate), with athletes representing over 19 countries. The field comprised 8,559 men and 1,560 women (15.4% female). The average finish time was 10:03:09.\n\nMedals awarded: 20 Gold, 506 Silver, 1,927 Bill Rowan, 5,036 Bronze, 2,630 Vic Clapham. 1,802 runners (17.8%) were completing their first Comrades. The final finisher was Thamsanqa ZUMA in 11:59:59.\n\nVeterans and masters athletes made up 49% of the finishers, with 5,116 seniors (avg 09:49:04) and 5,003 in the veteran categories.","countryDataPct":100.0}